  body: `Prior Lessons — 1-Sentence Recap

Lesson 090: Open chip interfaces still need qualified controller, physical-layer and verification IP before they work reliably in silicon.

Lesson 091: A durable control point forms where one supplier repeatedly turns several layers into useful output that customers cannot easily reproduce.

Lesson 092: Higher rack-distribution voltage can relieve copper constraints while moving scarcity toward protection, qualification and service.

